## Commands

```bash
# Install dependencies
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile

# Development
pnpm dev                    # Start dev server (http://localhost:5173)

# Build & Deploy
pnpm build                  # Production build
pnpm start                  # Local production preview via Wrangler

# Database
pnpm db:generate            # Generate Drizzle migrations
pnpm db:migrate:local       # Apply migrations to local D1

# Quality
pnpm typecheck              # TypeScript check
pnpm test                   # Run 35 automated tests
pnpm lint                   # ESLint

# CI (GitHub Actions)
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile → pnpm typecheck → pnpm test → pnpm build
```

---

## Testing

- **35 automated tests** covering:
  - Pure domain logic (risk rules, positive/negative cases)
  - Full API/service workflow integration
  - Authorization and tenant isolation
  - Concurrency and optimistic locking
  - Failure recovery and safe retries
  - 1,000-row CSV import stress test
  - CSV export formula injection protection
- Tests use **disposable in-memory SQLite databases** — no external dependencies
- Native **Node.js test runner** (no Jest/Vitest dependency)

---

## Architecture Highlights

- **Single deployable** — Modular monolith, not microservices
- **Clean separation** — `domain.ts` (pure logic) → `service.ts` (use cases) → `repository.ts` (SQL)
- **Tenant isolation** — All queries scoped by workspace ID derived from authenticated identity
- **Transactional batches** — D1 batch API for atomic multi-statement operations
- **Evidence integrity** — Evidence changes invalidate stale decisions and executions
- **Optimistic concurrency** — Version checks prevent lost updates across all mutable entities

---

## Prototype Boundaries

- All connectors are **simulations** — no real external permissions are modified
- Scans and execution are **user-triggered** — no background scheduler
- Policies use **transparent rules**, not ML/AI models
- Client-side pagination/filtering (not server-side)
- Audit records are application-protected but not cryptographically immutable
- No penetration test or compliance certification performed

